{"actions":[],"cardId":"cardid_3499b675ea28cbd97d56d82fa30f46b2","createdAt":"2026-03-14T01:05:22Z","expiresAt":"2026-03-16T01:05:22Z","icon":"square.grid.2x2","id":"card_9c76dcacd29d8232d3efa7a972f4293a","message":"Neuracle’s NEO system is the first invasive brain-computer interface cleared for commercial clinical use anywhere in the world — beating Neuralink to market.","metadata":{"height":520,"htmlContent":"<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width,initial-scale=1'><meta name='color-scheme' content='light dark'><style>:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#ffffff);--text:var(--fw-text,#111827);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#6b7280);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#9ca3af);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(15,23,42,0.08));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#2563eb);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#f3f4f6)}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#1c1c1e);--text:var(--fw-text,#f2f2f7);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#a0a0a0);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#707070);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(255,255,255,0.1));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#4b93ff);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#2a2a2a)}}body{margin:0;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--text);background:var(--bg)}*{box-sizing:border-box}a.card-link{display:block;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;cursor:pointer}a.card-link:active{opacity:0.7}.hero-img{width:100%;height:clamp(120px,34vw,220px);object-fit:cover;display:block;background:var(--border)}.content{padding:16px 20px 20px}.headline{font-size:18px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3;margin:0 0 6px;color:var(--text)}.source{font-size:13px;color:var(--tertiary);font-weight:500;margin:0 0 10px}.summary{font-size:15px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 14px}.stats{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap}.stat{background:var(--surface);padding:8px 12px;border-radius:8px;font-size:12px;line-height:1.3}.stat-val{font-weight:700;font-size:14px;color:var(--text);display:block;margin-bottom:2px}.stat-lbl{color:var(--tertiary)}</style></head><body><a class='card-link' href='https://freshfromchina.com/china-just-approved-the-worlds-first-invasive-brain-computer-interface-for-clinical-use-heres-what-it-means/' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'><img class='hero-img' src='https://abit.ee/images/neuracle-bci-brain-computer-interface-china-nmpa-neuralink-neurotechnology-2026-01.webp' alt='Neuracle BCI device' onerror=\"this.style.display='none'\"><div class='content'><div class='headline'>China Wins the BCI Race</div><div class='source'>FreshFromChina · Mar 13, 2026</div><div class='summary'>Neuracle’s NEO system is the first invasive brain-computer interface cleared for commercial clinical use anywhere in the world. Developed with Tsinghua University, it restores hand function for quadriplegic patients using semi-invasive epidural electrodes and wireless data transmission. Neuralink remains in clinical trials. BCI stocks surged 10%+ on Chinese exchanges.</div><div class='stats'><div class='stat'><span class='stat-val'>$97–139K</span><span class='stat-lbl'>Cost per unit</span></div><div class='stat'><span class='stat-val'>$16B</span><span class='stat-lbl'>China BCI market by 2040</span></div><div class='stat'><span class='stat-val'>1st</span><span class='stat-lbl'>Commercial invasive BCI</span></div></div></div></a></body></html>","web_images":[{"image_url":"https://freshfromchina.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/1773405461.png","source_url":"https://freshfromchina.com/china-just-approved-the-worlds-first-invasive-brain-computer-interface-for-clinical-use-heres-what-it-means"}]},"priority":"medium","state":"active","subType":"articles","subtitle":"FreshFromChina · Mar 13, 2026","timestamp":"2026-03-14T01:05:22Z","title":"China Wins the BCI Race","type":"html-webview"}
{"actions":[],"cardId":"cardid_7bd4a4917fc8e113c9d6874ce5e404d8","createdAt":"2026-03-14T01:05:22Z","expiresAt":"2026-03-16T01:05:22Z","icon":"square.grid.2x2","id":"card_9fbbb4aa0216961d722d16412f4656a6","message":"The SaaS-to-AI leadership transition pattern is accelerating. Narayen joins a growing list of long-tenured tech CEOs making way for AI-native successors.","metadata":{"height":420,"htmlContent":"<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width,initial-scale=1'><meta name='color-scheme' content='light dark'><style>:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#ffffff);--text:var(--fw-text,#111827);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#6b7280);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#9ca3af);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(15,23,42,0.08));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#2563eb);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#f3f4f6)}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#1c1c1e);--text:var(--fw-text,#f2f2f7);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#a0a0a0);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#707070);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(255,255,255,0.1));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#4b93ff);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#2a2a2a)}}body{margin:0;padding:20px;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--text);background:var(--bg)}*{box-sizing:border-box}h4{font-size:18px;margin:0 0 4px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3}.subtitle{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 10px;line-height:1.4}.msg{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.5}.divider{border:none;border-top:1px solid var(--border);margin:0}.point{padding:12px 0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.4}.point strong{font-weight:600}.point-detail{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin:2px 0 0}.num{font-size:28px;font-weight:700;color:var(--accent);margin:0 0 2px}.num-label{font-size:12px;color:var(--tertiary);margin:0 0 12px}.stats-row{display:flex;gap:16px;margin:0 0 16px}.stat-block{flex:1;text-align:center;padding:12px 8px;background:var(--surface);border-radius:10px}.stat-block .num{font-size:22px;line-height:1.2;color:var(--text)}.stat-block .num-label{margin:0}</style></head><body><h4>Adobe’s 18-year era ends</h4><div class='subtitle'>Shantanu Narayen steps down as CEO amid a $6.4B quarter and 8% stock drop</div><p class='msg'>The SaaS-to-AI leadership transition pattern is accelerating. Narayen joins a growing list of long-tenured tech CEOs making way for AI-native successors.</p><div class='stats-row'><div class='stat-block'><div class='num'>$6.4B</div><div class='num-label'>Q1 revenue</div></div><div class='stat-block'><div class='num'>−8%</div><div class='num-label'>Stock reaction</div></div><div class='stat-block'><div class='num'>18yr</div><div class='num-label'>Tenure</div></div></div><hr class='divider'><div class='point'><strong>The pivot paradox</strong><div class='point-detail'>Revenue beat by $120M, EPS beat at $6.06 vs $5.87 expected — yet the market punished Adobe on leadership uncertainty and soft Q2 guidance ($5.80–$5.85 EPS).</div></div><hr class='divider'><div class='point'><strong>AI cannibalization fear</strong><div class='point-detail'>Traditional stock business declining as AI-native tools from Canva, OpenAI, and others chip away at Creative Cloud’s legacy moats. The successor inherits a company that must dominate through engineering, not M&A.</div></div><hr class='divider'><div class='point'><strong>Pattern recognition</strong><div class='point-detail'>Gates at Microsoft, Jobs at Apple, now Narayen at Adobe. Each left during a platform shift. The next CEO will define whether Adobe leads or follows the generative AI era.</div></div></body></html>"},"priority":"medium","state":"active","subType":"insight","subtitle":"Shantanu Narayen steps down as CEO amid a $6.4B quarter and 8% stock drop","timestamp":"2026-03-14T01:05:22Z","title":"Adobe’s 18-year era ends","type":"html-webview"}
{"actions":[],"cardId":"cardid_64de6c49bb2eb9b42a3e07f8d00ab768","createdAt":"2026-03-14T01:05:22Z","expiresAt":"2026-03-16T01:05:22Z","icon":"square.grid.2x2","id":"card_c70eab597517c2abc8bd6266678baea3","message":"Three conference speakerphones under $300 that handle large rooms and outdoor use. All support daisy-chaining for round tables.","metadata":{"height":400,"htmlContent":"<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width,initial-scale=1'><meta name='color-scheme' content='light dark'><style>:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#ffffff);--text:var(--fw-text,#111827);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#6b7280);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#9ca3af);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(15,23,42,0.08));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#2563eb);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#f3f4f6)}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#1c1c1e);--text:var(--fw-text,#f2f2f7);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#a0a0a0);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#707070);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(255,255,255,0.1));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#4b93ff);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#2a2a2a)}}body{margin:0;padding:20px;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--text);background:var(--bg)}*{box-sizing:border-box}h4{font-size:18px;margin:0 0 4px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3}.subtitle{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 10px;line-height:1.4}.msg{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.5}.divider{border:none;border-top:1px solid var(--border);margin:0}.item{padding:14px 0}.item-name{font-size:15px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.3;margin:0 0 4px}.item-price{font-size:13px;color:var(--accent);font-weight:600;margin:0 0 4px}.item-detail{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.4;margin:0}.note{font-size:12px;color:var(--tertiary);margin:14px 0 0;padding:10px 12px;background:var(--surface);border-radius:8px;line-height:1.4}</style></head><body><h4>Finish the mic research</h4><div class='subtitle'>You asked about multi-mic round-table solutions last night — here’s a shortlist to start from</div><p class='msg'>Three conference speakerphones under $300 that handle large rooms and outdoor use. All support daisy-chaining for round tables.</p><hr class='divider'><div class='item'><div class='item-name'>Anker PowerConf S500</div><div class='item-price'>~$200</div><div class='item-detail'>360° voice pickup, link two units for 20-person tables, USB-C + Bluetooth. Battery-powered — works outdoors. Teams & Zoom certified.</div></div><hr class='divider'><div class='item'><div class='item-name'>Jabra Speak2 75</div><div class='item-price'>~$280</div><div class='item-detail'>Full duplex, 4-mic beamforming array, 30-hour battery. Link two wirelessly. Certified for Teams, Zoom, and Google Meet.</div></div><hr class='divider'><div class='item'><div class='item-name'>Konftel 55Wx</div><div class='item-price'>~$180</div><div class='item-detail'>OmniSound HD, USB/Bluetooth/NFC. Portable and battery-powered. Daisy-chain with expansion mics for larger coverage.</div></div><div class='note'>⚠️ For 6,000 sq ft outdoor coverage, two daisy-chained units placed on the table will help — but you’ll want to test wind noise. A dead-cat windscreen or sheltered spot matters more than mic specs outdoors. I can do deeper research when you’re ready.</div></body></html>"},"priority":"medium","state":"active","subType":"suggestions","subtitle":"You asked about multi-mic round-table solutions last night — here’s a shortlist to start from","timestamp":"2026-03-14T01:05:22Z","title":"Finish the mic research","type":"html-webview"}
