{"actions":[],"cardId":"cardid_3499b675ea28cbd97d56d82fa30f46b2","createdAt":"2026-03-14T01:05:22Z","expiresAt":"2026-03-16T01:05:22Z","icon":"square.grid.2x2","id":"card_8eb5f9d350ea0052fe05da1b6e55e88f","message":"The Pentagon’s options for keeping the world’s most critical oil chokepoint open — and why none of them are simple.","metadata":{"height":480,"htmlContent":"<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width,initial-scale=1'><meta name='color-scheme' content='light dark'><style>:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#ffffff);--text:var(--fw-text,#111827);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#6b7280);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#9ca3af);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(15,23,42,0.08));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#2563eb);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#f3f4f6)}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#1c1c1e);--text:var(--fw-text,#f2f2f7);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#a0a0a0);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#707070);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(255,255,255,0.1));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#4b93ff);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#2a2a2a)}}body{margin:0;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--text);background:var(--bg)}*{box-sizing:border-box}a.card-link{display:block;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;cursor:pointer}a.card-link:active{opacity:0.7}.hero{background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a2332 0%,#2d4a66 100%);padding:40px 20px 24px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px}.hero-label{font-size:11px;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.06em;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)}.hero-title{font-size:22px;font-weight:700;color:#fff;line-height:1.25;margin:0}.hero-sub{font-size:14px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);line-height:1.4;margin:0}.content{padding:16px 20px 20px}.summary{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0 0 14px}.key-facts{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px}.fact{background:var(--surface);padding:6px 10px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;color:var(--text);font-weight:500}</style></head><body><a class='card-link' href='https://news.usni.org/2026/03/10/operation-epic-escort' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'><div class='hero'><div class='hero-label'>Long read</div><div class='hero-title'>Operation Epic Escort</div><div class='hero-sub'>USNI News · Updated Mar 13, 2026</div></div><div class='content'><div class='summary'>The Pentagon’s options for keeping the world’s most critical oil chokepoint open — and why none of them are simple. From Mar 1–3, an intensifying conflict brought tanker traffic to a near-total halt. IRGC warnings, GPS jamming, war-risk insurance withdrawal, and strikes on 4 tankers and Iranian naval assets created unprecedented disruption. Shadow-fleet vessels now account for half of all strait transits. Iran selectively opened passage on Mar 13 for Turkish and Indian ships — a new geopolitical lever.</div><div class='key-facts'><span class='fact'>11 ships damaged</span><span class='fact'>10 seafarers killed/missing</span><span class='fact'>50% shadow fleet</span><span class='fact'>Oman ports struck by drones</span></div></div></a></body></html>"},"priority":"medium","state":"active","subType":"articles","subtitle":"USNI News · Updated Mar 13, 2026","timestamp":"2026-03-14T01:05:22Z","title":"Operation Epic Escort","type":"html-webview"}
